' Clicks on the leader (`preset classic ai none seed 3 start 30 party`: the
' leader and one companion handed over, a prepared state; in Paradise Camp
' the leader stands at 64,160, the companion at 63,147). v1.2's
' `GetObjectAt` counts the leader (`Party[0]`, MapViewOverlayCharacters.cs:
' 160-195) and `ClickCharacter` (LocationScene.cs:247-255) on one's own
' character calls `SelectCharacter`, false when he is already the selected
' one, and then `OnMenuInventory` (Player.cs:200-231). So: in group mode a
' click on the leader opens his inventory; with the companion selected it
' selects the leader alone; clicked again, his inventory. In fight mode
' nothing happens. Before, a click on him was a walk to his own feet.
press escape             ' Back closes the manual v1.2 opens on a new game's first world map (MapScene.cs:687-691)
mapclick 110,122         ' into Paradise Camp
wait 60
mapclick 64,156          ' the leader, in group mode: his inventory
wait 5
snap leader_inventory
esc
wait 5
clickfriend 1            ' the companion, alone
wait 5
mapclick 64,156          ' the leader: selected alone
wait 5
mapclick 64,156          ' again: his inventory
wait 5
esc
wait 5
fight                    ' fight mode
mapclick 64,156          ' nothing
wait 5
save                     ' he has not moved: 64,160
quit
